.TH std::expected::value_or 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::expected::value_or \- std::expected::value_or

.SH Synopsis
Primary template
template< class U >                               \fB(1)\fP (since C++23)
constexpr T value_or( U&& default_value ) const&;
template< class U >                               \fB(2)\fP (since C++23)
constexpr T value_or( U&& default_value ) &&;

Returns the expected value if it exists, otherwise returns default_value.

The void partial specialization does not have these member functions.

1) If std::is_copy_constructible_v<T> or std::is_convertible_v<U, T> is false, the program
is ill-formed.
2) If std::is_move_constructible_v<T> or std::is_convertible_v<U, T> is false, the program
is ill-formed.

.SH Parameters

default_value - the value to use in case *this does not contain an expected value

.SH Return value

1) has_value() ? **this : static_cast<T>(std::forward<U>(default_value))
2) has_value() ? std::move(**this) : static_cast<T>(std::forward<U>(default_value))

